989
00:37:00.850 --> 00:37:05.690
I don't know if you guys also noticed behind Jan's chair, there's a little table and on
有一个删减片段是迈克尔告诉菲利斯他想要鹳鸟。

990
00:37:05.690 --> 00:37:07.930
the table is a big bird stuffed animal.
她说她弄不到鹳鸟。

991
00:37:08.190 --> 00:37:11.910
There is a deleted scene where Michael tells Phyllis he wants storks.
然后他说，听着，我好不容易才让简今天过来。

992
00:37:12.110 --> 00:37:13.890
She said she couldn't get storks.
这必须是一场盛大的派对。

993
00:37:13.930 --> 00:37:16.530
And he's like, look, I barely got Jan to even come today.
如果你弄不到鹳鸟，我至少想要大鸟。

994
00:37:16.750 --> 00:37:18.250
This needs to be a big party.
菲利斯能做到的最好结果就是弄到了一个大鸟玩偶。

995
00:37:18.550 --> 00:37:21.110
If you can't get a stork, I at least want big bird.
哇。

996
00:37:21.310 --> 00:37:24.410
And the best Phyllis could do is she got a big bird stuffed animal.
是啊。

997
00:37:25.070 --> 00:37:25.530
Wow.
噢，那太棒了。

998
00:37:25.970 --> 00:37:26.310
Yeah.
嗯，大家开始给简送礼物了。

999
00:37:26.990 --> 00:37:28.370
Oh, that is so great.
这真是太棒了。

1000
00:37:28.730 --> 00:37:31.430
Well, the group gives Jan her gift.
好吧，大家把礼物送给了简。

1001
00:37:31.650 --> 00:37:32.750
It's a stroller.
那是一辆婴儿车。

1002
00:37:33.050 --> 00:37:34.910
I think this is a very nice gift.
我觉得这是一份非常棒的礼物。

1003
00:37:35.090 --> 00:37:37.810
It's a very nice gift because it's a big ticket item.
这是一份非常棒的礼物，因为它是件大件贵重物品。

1004
00:37:37.970 --> 00:37:39.750
But she's already got a stroller.
但她已经有一辆婴儿车了。

1005
00:37:40.010 --> 00:37:41.350
She has an orbit.
她有一辆Orbit牌的。

1006
00:37:41.710 --> 00:37:44.510
That Oscar tells us costs $1,200.
奥斯卡告诉我们那辆要1200美元。

1007
00:37:45.410 --> 00:37:45.770
Yeah.
是啊。

1008
00:37:46.590 --> 00:37:47.970
Dwight is curious.
德怀特很好奇。

1009
00:37:47.970 --> 00:37:51.350
He's like, I need to see how good this stroller really is.
他心想，我得看看这辆婴儿车到底有多好。

1010
00:37:51.350 --> 00:37:56.550
Yeah, he said his whole bomb shelter bunker thing that he built didn't even cost that much.
没错，他说他建的那个防空洞地堡都没花那么多钱。

1011
00:37:56.950 --> 00:38:00.970
And he needs to see what the stroller is made of, if it's going to cost that much.
而且他得看看这婴儿车到底是什么做的，才值那么多钱。

1012
00:38:01.270 --> 00:38:04.010
So, yeah, he wheels the stroller out.
所以，没错，他把婴儿车推了出去。

1013
00:38:04.110 --> 00:38:07.790
And then Jan is going to sing to the baby.
然后简要给宝宝唱歌。

1014
00:38:08.270 --> 00:38:09.130
Oh, Jenna.
噢，珍娜。

1015
00:38:09.430 --> 00:38:11.510
How did you get through this?
你是怎么熬过这一段的？

1016
00:38:11.650 --> 00:38:12.550
How did you get through it?
你是怎么熬过来的？

1017
00:38:12.550 --> 00:38:16.170
It was like, bite the inside of your cheek.
当时就像是，咬住自己的腮帮子内侧。

1018
00:38:16.310 --> 00:38:18.210
Don't make eye contact with anyone.
别和任何人有眼神交流。

1019
00:38:18.410 --> 00:38:23.370
And also, at the same time, in total awe of Melora.
而且同时，对梅洛拉感到无比敬佩。

1020
00:38:23.710 --> 00:38:24.130
Yes.
没错。

1021
00:38:24.230 --> 00:38:27.790
Who has an amazing singing voice and performs as a singer, guys.
她有一副惊人的歌喉，而且本身就是位歌手，伙计们。

1022
00:38:27.910 --> 00:38:28.190
Yes.
没错。

1023
00:38:28.310 --> 00:38:29.290
She has albuMs.
她出过专辑。

1024
00:38:29.610 --> 00:38:29.890
Yes.
没错。

1025
00:38:30.030 --> 00:38:31.130
She's an amazing singer.
她是一位了不起的歌手。

1026
00:38:31.350 --> 00:38:34.750
She just owned this moment so wholeheartedly.
她全心全意地掌控了那一刻。

1027
00:38:34.970 --> 00:38:38.370
There is a scene, Jenna, that was in the script that we shot.
珍娜，剧本里有一场我们拍过的戏。

1028
00:38:38.370 --> 00:38:42.790
I remember shooting it because the timing and everything in it was amazing.
我记得拍那场戏的时候，因为里面的节奏和一切都太棒了。

1029
00:38:43.630 --> 00:38:45.830
So, Jan is singing Son of a Preacher Man.
当时简在唱《牧师之子》。

1030
00:38:45.830 --> 00:38:47.090
She's belting it out.
她唱得声嘶力竭。

1031
00:38:47.250 --> 00:38:49.450
And Ryan comes in urgently to tell her something.
然后瑞安急匆匆地进来想告诉她什么。

1032
00:38:49.790 --> 00:38:51.010
She won't stop singing.
她却不停下来。

1033
00:38:51.850 --> 00:38:53.750
And I printed out the script.
我把剧本打印出来了。

1034
00:38:53.890 --> 00:38:55.250
Here, Jenna, just read right here.
给你，珍娜，就读这里。

1035
00:38:55.590 --> 00:38:55.790
Okay.
好的。

1036
00:38:55.950 --> 00:38:56.970
So, I'm going to be Ryan.
那我来演瑞安。

1037
00:38:57.150 --> 00:38:57.330
Yeah.
好。

1038
00:38:57.610 --> 00:38:57.890
Okay.
好的。

1039
00:38:58.090 --> 00:38:59.530
And you guys forgive my singing.
大家请原谅我的歌声。

1040
00:38:59.690 --> 00:39:00.290
I'm not a singer.
我不是歌手。

1041
00:39:00.410 --> 00:39:00.570
Okay.
好的。

1042
00:39:01.190 --> 00:39:03.130
Was the Son of a Preacher Man.
那是位牧师之子。

1043
00:39:03.150 --> 00:39:04.230
Yes, he was.
是的，他是。

1044
00:39:04.450 --> 00:39:04.870
Hey, Jan.
嘿，简。

1045
00:39:05.070 --> 00:39:05.810
He was.
他是。

1046
00:39:05.950 --> 00:39:06.170
Jan.
简。

1047
00:39:06.350 --> 00:39:07.270
Yes, he was.
是的，他是。

1048
00:39:07.270 --> 00:39:09.250
You parked in the handicapped spot.
你停在残疾人车位上了。

1049
00:39:09.490 --> 00:39:11.410
Keys are in my purse.
钥匙在我的包里。

1050
00:39:11.610 --> 00:39:12.430
I'll just, I'll take them.
我这就去，我去拿钥匙。

1051
00:39:13.150 --> 00:39:14.190
Did I do good?
我表现得好吗？

1052
00:39:14.390 --> 00:39:15.310
You did great.
你表现得太棒了。

1053
00:39:15.690 --> 00:39:17.750
Sorry to make you guys suffer through my singing.
抱歉让你们忍受我的歌声。

1054
00:39:17.910 --> 00:39:18.810
Melora was amazing.
梅洛拉唱得太棒了。

1055
00:39:18.990 --> 00:39:20.130
She never missed a beat.
她节奏感把握得非常好。

1056
00:39:20.390 --> 00:39:22.870
She sang where her keys were.
她唱得非常符合她的音域。

1057
00:39:23.430 --> 00:39:24.410
It was amazing.
真是太棒了。

1058
00:39:24.790 --> 00:39:28.330
I did a mini deep dive on Son of a Preacher Man.
我稍微深入研究了一下《牧师之子》。

1059
00:39:28.530 --> 00:39:29.230
Did you really?
真的吗？

1060
00:39:29.410 --> 00:39:29.810
Yes.
是的。

1061
00:39:30.010 --> 00:39:31.510
I think we should take a break.
我觉得我们该休息一下了。

1062
00:39:31.510 --> 00:39:33.750
And when we come back, I'll tell you what I found.
等我们回来，我会告诉你们我的发现。

1063
00:39:33.970 --> 00:39:34.230
Okay.
好的。

1064
00:39:44.960 --> 00:39:45.540
All right.
没问题。

1065
00:39:45.660 --> 00:39:46.460
We are back.
我们回来了。

1066
00:39:46.460 --> 00:39:51.820
And I'm going to start us off with a fan question from Yvette M and Alexandra S.
首先，我来回答一个来自伊薇特·M和亚历山德拉·S的粉丝提问。

1067
00:39:52.060 --> 00:39:56.860
Why was the song Son of a Preacher Man chosen for Jan to sing to her baby?
为什么选《牧师之子》这首歌让简唱给她的宝宝听？

1068
00:39:57.120 --> 00:39:59.380
I asked Aaron who picked the song.
我问了亚伦是谁选的这首歌。

1069
00:39:59.620 --> 00:40:05.480
And Aaron said he isn't sure if Mindy picked it per se, but she was pushing it.
亚伦说他不确定是不是敏迪选的，但确实是她在力推。

1070
00:40:05.600 --> 00:40:08.840
He said, I don't remember how exactly it came up in the writer's room.
他说，我不记得在编剧室里具体是怎么提出来的了。

1071
00:40:09.020 --> 00:40:12.280
But the minute it was out there, Mindy was like, that's got to be it.
但一旦提出来，敏迪就说，就是这首了。

1072
00:40:12.280 --> 00:40:13.720
That has got to be it.
非它莫属。

1073
00:40:14.180 --> 00:40:16.560
So I think we have Mindy to thank for that.
所以我认为我们得感谢敏迪。

1074
00:40:16.740 --> 00:40:20.120
I got curious about the song, so I did a little deep dive on it.
我对这首歌产生了好奇，所以我做了一点深入研究。

1075
00:40:20.500 --> 00:40:24.800
Son of a Preacher Man was written by John Hurley and Ronnie Wilkins.
《牧师之子》是由约翰·赫尔利和罗尼·威尔金斯创作的。

1076
00:40:25.100 --> 00:40:28.840
It was recorded by Dusty Springfield in 1968.
它由达斯蒂·斯普林菲尔德在1968年录制。

1077
00:40:28.840 --> 00:40:31.620
And her version is most popular.
她的版本是最受欢迎的。

1078
00:40:31.620 --> 00:40:34.080
It's been covered many times by many artists.
这首歌被许多艺术家翻唱过很多次。

1079
00:40:34.500 --> 00:40:36.180
Here's what I found interesting.
以下是我觉得有趣的地方。

1080
00:40:36.800 --> 00:40:42.620
Apparently, the rights to record the song were originally offered to Aretha Franklin.
显然，这首歌的录制版权最初是提供给艾瑞莎·弗兰克林的。

1081
00:40:42.940 --> 00:40:44.940
She was the daughter of a preacher.
她本人就是一位牧师的女儿。

1082
00:40:45.320 --> 00:40:50.940
And the rumor is that she turned it down because she worried that maybe it might be a little disrespectful.
传闻说她拒绝了，因为她担心这首歌可能会有点不敬。

1083
00:40:51.280 --> 00:40:52.620
But she changed her mind.
但她后来改变了主意。

1084
00:40:53.040 --> 00:40:53.400
No.
不。

1085
00:40:53.400 --> 00:40:59.500
And she recorded a cover version of the song just one year later in 1969 for her album Soul Sister.
她在一年后的1969年为她的专辑《灵魂姐妹》录制了这首歌的翻唱版本。

1086
00:40:59.860 --> 00:41:01.380
I had to hear it.
我一定要听听看。

1087
00:41:01.700 --> 00:41:02.940
Sam, will you play it?
山姆，能放一下吗？

1088
00:41:34.040 --> 00:41:35.660
It's so good, isn't it?
太好听了，不是吗？

1089
00:41:35.780 --> 00:41:36.100
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1090
00:41:36.340 --> 00:41:37.740
She always gives me chills.
她总是让我起鸡皮疙瘩。

1091
00:41:38.220 --> 00:41:41.560
Dolly Parton also did a cover in 1996 for her album Treasures.
多莉·帕顿也在1996年为她的专辑《珍宝》翻唱过这首歌。

1092
00:41:41.680 --> 00:41:43.360
And it is also a gem.
那也是一首瑰宝。

1093
00:41:43.540 --> 00:41:44.460
Do you want to hear that one?
你想听听那个版本吗？

1094
00:41:44.620 --> 00:41:45.100
Yes.
想。

1095
00:41:46.900 --> 00:41:49.000
Billy Ray was a preacher's son.
比利·雷是牧师的儿子。

1096
00:41:49.000 --> 00:41:51.540
And when his daddy would visit, he'd come along.
每当他爸爸来访，他也会跟着来。

1097
00:41:52.200 --> 00:41:57.300
When they gathered around and started talking, that's when Billy would take me walking.
当他们聚在一起聊天时，比利就会带我出去散步。

1098
00:41:57.740 --> 00:42:00.100
Through the backyard we'd go walking.
我们会在后院散步。

1099
00:42:00.660 --> 00:42:02.720
Billy looked into my eyes.
比利注视着我的双眼。

1100
00:42:11.510 --> 00:42:12.550
I mean, just—
我是说，简直——

1101
00:42:12.550 --> 00:42:14.550
I can listen to these women sing anything.
我愿意听这些女士唱任何歌。

1102
00:42:14.690 --> 00:42:15.630
They're legends.
她们是传奇。

1103
00:42:16.050 --> 00:42:18.170
Legends in our podcast today.
今天做客我们播客的传奇人物。

1104
00:42:18.490 --> 00:42:20.210
Do we need to hear Dusty's?
我们有必要听达斯蒂唱的版本吗？

1105
00:42:20.650 --> 00:42:22.470
I think we need to hear Dusty's.
我觉得我们有必要听听达斯蒂的版本。

1106
00:42:22.550 --> 00:42:24.130
I mean, we have to hear Dusty's.
我是说，我们必须得听听达斯蒂的版本。

1107
00:42:24.130 --> 00:42:26.250
It's Son of a Preacher Man Day today.
今天是《牧师之子》主题日。

1108
00:42:26.450 --> 00:42:28.310
I mean, I just want to hear all of them.
我是说，我只想把她们唱的所有版本都听一遍。

1109
00:42:31.090 --> 00:42:35.890
I feel so embarrassed that I even attempted to sing it at all to recreate the scene with Ryan.
我真为自己当初为了重现和瑞安的那场戏而尝试去唱它感到尴尬。

1110
00:42:36.170 --> 00:42:37.290
I am so sorry.
我真的很抱歉。

1111
00:43:03.770 --> 00:43:04.790
Oh, so good.
噢，太棒了。

1112
00:43:04.990 --> 00:43:05.250
All right.
好吧。

1113
00:43:05.350 --> 00:43:05.650
All right.
好吧。

1114
00:43:05.650 --> 00:43:07.190
Here's what I have to say.
我有话要说。

1115
00:43:07.430 --> 00:43:09.770
Kudos to John Hurley and Ronnie Wilkins,
向约翰·赫利和罗尼·威尔金斯致敬，

1116
00:43:09.810 --> 00:43:17.790
because when you write a song that can be sung by all of these different people with their different spins on it and their different arrangements—
因为当你写出一首能被这么多不同的人演唱，且每个人都能唱出自己的风格和编曲，

1117
00:43:17.790 --> 00:43:20.550
And it still knocks your socks off every time.
而且每次听都依然能让人惊艳不已时，

1118
00:43:20.650 --> 00:43:21.870
You have written a good song.
你就写出了一首好歌。

1119
00:43:22.010 --> 00:43:22.150
Yep.
没错。

1120
00:43:22.550 --> 00:43:30.190
One last thing I want to say about Son of a Preacher Man is that when Melora sang it, she improvised the snapping.
关于《牧师之子》，我最后想说的是，梅洛拉演唱时，那个打响指的动作是她即兴发挥的。

1121
00:43:30.730 --> 00:43:31.870
And you know what?
你猜怎么着？

1122
00:43:31.870 --> 00:43:34.750
But it about got me on the floor.
那简直让我笑得瘫倒在地。

1123
00:43:34.950 --> 00:43:41.770
We were so trying to suppress laughter that one more thing was like the tipping point, you know?
我们当时拼命忍着笑，再多一点点诱因就会彻底破功，你懂吗？

1124
00:43:41.930 --> 00:43:42.170
Yes.
懂。

1125
00:43:42.170 --> 00:43:48.030
And so as she's swaying and singing, when she just starts doing that snap, I was like, oh, Lord, I'm not going to make it.
所以当她摇摆着身体唱歌，突然开始打响指时，我心想，天哪，我快撑不住了。

1126
00:43:48.170 --> 00:43:49.150
I am not going to make it.
我真的要撑不住了。

1127
00:43:49.470 --> 00:43:54.130
There are really great scripted talking heads of people reacting to it.
剧本里确实有一些很棒的采访片段，记录了人们对此的反应。

1128
00:43:54.250 --> 00:43:57.950
And Stan Lee had a great one where he was like, I used to like that song.
斯坦·李就有一个很棒的片段，他说他以前挺喜欢那首歌的。

1129
00:44:01.760 --> 00:44:04.580
Well, Jim is going to try to describe it to Pam.
嗯，吉姆当时正试图向帕姆描述这件事。

1130
00:44:05.200 --> 00:44:08.720
She's at the laundromat, and she can't hear anything he's saying.
她在洗衣店，根本听不清他在说什么。

1131
00:44:08.980 --> 00:44:11.320
Why couldn't she just walk away from the machines, Jenna?
珍娜，她为什么就不能从洗衣机旁边走开呢？

1132
00:44:11.320 --> 00:44:12.080
You know what?
你知道吗？

1133
00:44:12.200 --> 00:44:12.740
Megan P.
梅根·P.

1134
00:44:12.800 --> 00:44:15.040
would like to know the answer to that question as well.
也想知道这个问题的答案。

1135
00:44:15.200 --> 00:44:15.920
Megan, it's the first thing I thought.
梅根，这也是我第一个想到的问题。

1136
00:44:16.060 --> 00:44:17.220
She hasn't talked to him all day.
她一整天都没跟他说话。

1137
00:44:17.320 --> 00:44:18.660
She finally has free time.
好不容易有了空闲时间。

1138
00:44:18.880 --> 00:44:20.260
Walk away from the machine.
走开啊，离开那台机器。

1139
00:44:20.640 --> 00:44:22.660
I'll tell you two things.
我告诉你们两点原因。

1140
00:44:22.900 --> 00:44:27.260
Number one, right before this phone call, there was a bit of the scene that got clipped.
第一，就在这通电话之前，有一小段戏被剪掉了。

1141
00:44:28.020 --> 00:44:34.440
Pam is with her friend at the laundromat, and they are together, and they're talking about a class assignment.
帕姆当时和她的朋友在洗衣店，她们在一起讨论课堂作业。

1142
00:44:34.640 --> 00:44:37.800
And she says, oh, just one second, I'm going to take this call.
然后她说，噢，等一下，我要接个电话。

1143
00:44:38.000 --> 00:44:41.140
So maybe she felt like she couldn't walk away.
所以也许她觉得没法走开。

1144
00:44:41.320 --> 00:44:50.360
But also in the script, there is a version where she does walk away from the machines, and the problem is not that the machines are loud.
